# Test case format

When creating or editing any test under `tests/specs/` (or any `*.spec.ts` in this repo):

1. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/writing-test-cases/SKILL.md` first.
2. Use titles matching `should <expected result> when <condition>`.
3. Structure each test with `test.step()` blocks named `Input Data: ...` (optional), `Action: ...` (required), and `Validation: ...` (required), in that order.
4. Put every `expect` inside a `Validation:` step only.
5. Import `test` / `expect` from `tests/src/fixtures`, not directly from `@playwright/test`.
6. Run `npm run lint:tests` from `tests/` before considering the work done.
